 34	// This file holds the observation tools — read, grep, glob, ls, and check.
 35	// None of them changes anything, so none of them asks for confirmation, and
 36	// each answers immediately rather than being batched like the edits.
 37	//
 38	// Every result is written for a reader who cannot see the terminal: it says
 39	// what was searched, what was found, and — when a limit cut the answer short —
 40	// that there is more. A silently truncated result reads as "nothing else
 41	// exists" and sends the next step down the wrong path.
 42	
 43	// maxToolOutputBytes caps a single tool result. Beyond this the result is cut
 44	// with a note, because one runaway command must not eat the context window.
 45	// maxGrepContext bounds one call's appetite for surrounding lines. Ten either
 46	// side is already a screenful per match; past that the file itself is what is
 47	// wanted, and read exists for that.
 48	const maxGrepContext = 20
 49	
 50	const maxToolOutputBytes = 60_000
