220	// globSyntaxNote explains the two glob shapes that silently admit nothing. Both
221	// are natural first guesses, and both used to fail to an empty result that named
222	// only the pattern, so a reader concluded the code was not there.
223	const globSyntaxNote = "A glob is matched against the whole path, segment by segment. " +
224		"\"*.go\" therefore matches only files in the project root, and a bare directory name " +
225		"matches nothing at all; use \"**/*.go\" to reach every directory. To search one subtree, " +
